      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T13:37:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think my preference would be for a macro that is either a no-op or that inserts the scoping object variable behind the scenes. This is mostly because its capitalization matches what we\u0027d do for a pointer field that is being excluded from raw_ptr conversion. It is a bit annoying to have it introducing a local variable name that theoretically could conflict with something else in the function block, but if we do something more unique than `exclusion` like `__miracleObjExclusion` I think that\u0027s safe.\n\nI would also prefer that the macro name reflect that these safety checks are specific to MiracleObj or the use of PartitionAlloc, such `SK_SCOPED_DISABLE_PARTIION_ALLOC_SAFETY_CHECKS`",
